## Governance

Govna makes recurring publishing ceremonies more effective and efficient by keeping settled intent, authority, scope, and proof reusable across phases and sessions. It automates deterministic mechanics while leaving decision-bearing choices and every gate with the Director.

[`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md) states the working rules for human Directors and agent Operators. [`govna/operator-contract-rationale.md`](govna/operator-contract-rationale.md) explains why those session-entry rules exist.

## AC Workflow

An acceptance-criteria document defines one bounded content change, its scope, and its tests. The short label AC refers both to that document and to the change it tracks.

Use `Draft → Audit → Refine → Implement → Ratify → Package` for an active AC. Draft writes the document. Audit challenges it without edits. Refine resolves findings in the document. Implement makes and verifies the settled content change. Ratify performs final acceptance review. Package prepares the accepted change for release. Lowercase phase names and `package`, `pack`, or `prep` carry the same workflow meanings. Ordinary coding phrases such as `build`, `prepare the build`, and `package the binary` do not advance the workflow.

An explicit agent-mediated request to run `govna audit` also authorizes immediate Audit and Refine for one emitted or reused adoption AC. The executable performs only deterministic comparison and emission. The Operator pauses for every blocker, resumes Refine after each blocker is resolved, runs Pre-Implementation Verification, and stops before Implement. A clean result or pre-emission failure enters no AC phase. A correction to the immutable AC requires a new audit emission.

Audit, Refine, Implement, and Ratify target one eligible AC. The pending release batch contains every unpackaged AC whose implementation is present, including work still awaiting Ratify. Before another AC enters Implement, the Operator privately checks that the projected plus-joined references and a brief result summary can fit one 80-byte message; that calculation does not start Package. Package requires every pending member to be Ratified and targets the complete batch. Use `Package AC70+AC71` to establish a fitting multi-AC batch. Use standalone `Package`, `package`, `pack`, or `prep` after a complete batch is known. Prep rejects an oversized batch, a partial batch, and a smaller batch that would leave implemented work outside the release.
